  "molecular-oncology": "Molecular Oncology, an open access journal of the Federation of European Biochemical Societies published by Wiley, spans basic and clinical cancer research plus policy pieces on prevention and care.",
  "nar-cancer": "NAR Cancer, the cancer sister journal of Nucleic Acids Research from Oxford University Press, publishes open access papers on DNA, RNA and genomics in cancer, including data resource articles.",
  neoplasia: "Neoplasia is an open access Elsevier journal for laboratory and translational cancer research across all tumour types, and encourages sharing of the cell lines and reagents it describes.",
  neoplasma: "Neoplasma is a Slovak English-language cancer journal, edited by the Cancer Research Institute of the Slovak Academy of Sciences, covering experimental oncology, clinical oncology and cancer epidemiology.",
  "nutrition-and-cancer": "Nutrition and Cancer, published by Routledge, reports how diet and nutrients affect cancer risk, treatment and prevention, from laboratory studies of how cancers start to dietetics and food policy.",
  "oncogene-journal": "Oncogene is a long-running cancer biology journal from the Nature stable, publishing molecular and cellular research on how cancers arise, spread and resist treatment for laboratory researchers.",
  oncoimmunology: "OncoImmunology is an open access Taylor & Francis journal devoted to the immune system's role in cancer and to immunotherapy, read by tumour immunologists and clinicians developing immune-based treatments.",
  "oncology-williston-park": "ONCOLOGY, listed in PubMed as Oncology (Williston Park), is an American clinical review journal for practising cancer doctors, now part of the CancerNetwork site run by MJH Life Sciences.",
  "oncology-karger": "Oncology is a Swiss clinical cancer journal from Karger in Basel, running since 1967, that carries clinical studies, translational research and short trial reports for oncologists.",
  "oncology-nursing-forum": "Oncology Nursing Forum is the journal of the Oncology Nursing Society in the United States, read by cancer nurses for studies on symptom management, care delivery and health equity.",
  "oncology-reports": "Oncology Reports is a Greek-based monthly journal from Spandidos Publications covering basic and applied cancer research, with a focus on how cancers start and spread, for laboratory researchers.",
